# /watch is the new name for the personalised FILM PLAYER (yours.html), renamed
# 2026-09-15 because THREE different things were called "yours" and it caused a
# real mix-up (someone nearly retired the wrong page):
#   /watch          this film player, showing an example film. Renamed.
#   /yours/<slug>   per-couple package pages in the yours/ DIRECTORY
#                   (taylor-justin, taylor-neil). Untouched.
#   prep.flyiniris.com/yours/<slug>   the personal package page. Untouched.
#
# This is a 200 REWRITE, not a 301, and deliberately so:
#   - /yours must keep working PERMANENTLY. Those links are in nurture emails
#     already sitting in real couples' inboxes, and email links are forever.
#     A rewrite leaves /yours serving exactly as it does today, zero hops.
#   - Renaming yours.html to watch.html would risk a clean-URL strip conflict
#     with the /yours/ DIRECTORY above, the same hazard that forced the
#     agreement shells into /_shells/.
#   - yours.html is noindex,nofollow and absent from sitemap.xml, so two paths
#     serving it costs nothing in search.
# Target is /yours, NOT /yours.html. Pages strips .html as a clean-URL
# normalisation, and a rewrite pointed at /yours.html comes back out as a 308
# redirect to /yours, which would bounce the visitor off /watch entirely and
# defeat the rename. Measured 2026-09-15 with wrangler pages dev.
# Query string is preserved by Cloudflare Pages since the destination has no
# ? clause, same as the /contract.html and /payment rules above. That matters:
# the page reads fn, vn, wd, film, fc and fv, and Sean attributes on utm_*.
/watch                     /yours       200
